---
Switch check: read /workspace/peptide/context/routines-on.md. If "Weekly creative brief" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time ET> · Weekly creative brief · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/peptide/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to Chris only, never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST".
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/peptide/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/peptide/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time ET> · Weekly creative brief · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Never use another bot's files, logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. If nothing changed, append "<time ET> · Weekly creative brief · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time ET> · Weekly creative brief · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/peptide/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

Use the ad-account-pulse skill, section Monday creative brief. Draft ten hooks and angles and three full ad concepts from this week's call objections, the Scale Advisor's latest memo in /workspace/peptide/vault/Advisor/Memos/ and the ads winning now.
Check every concept against the ad platform's policy for this category and the "Claims we never make" list in /workspace/peptide/context/offer.md. Drop any that fail.
Save the brief to /workspace/peptide/vault/Ads/Briefs/<week>.md and as a new Google Doc, and send Chris the link and the top three hooks. Publish nothing.
